# Secrets. The service's .env holds your OpenRouter API key.
service/.env
.env

# Python
service/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kb/ — your knowledge base. The folder ships; its contents never do.
#
# It holds your name, email, phone, employment history, resume, and every
# answer you have ever given. This repository is public, so none of that is
# tracked. The empty directory is kept so a fresh clone has somewhere to put a
# knowledge base, and the service creates the rest on first run.
#
# Keeping the data in version control is genuinely useful — you can see what an
# answer used to say and get it back. Do that in a SEPARATE private repository,
# or make this one private and delete these three lines.
kb/*
!kb/.gitkeep

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE ON kb/
#
# kb/ IS tracked on purpose: it is your knowledge base, and its history is the
# useful part — you can see what an answer used to say and get it back.
#
# It also contains personal data: your name, email, phone, employment history,
# every answer you have given, and your resume PDF. That is fine in a local or
# private repository. Do not push it to a public one.
#
# To keep the code in git but not the data, uncomment:
# kb/
